meta {
  name: Chat Completion (Tool Refs + Lineage)
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/gateway/chat/completions
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{apiKey}}
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "model": "{{model}}",
    "messages": [
      { "role": "user", "content": "What's the weather in Lisbon right now?" }
    ],
    "tool_refs": [
      { "name": "{{toolName}}", "alias": "production" }
    ],
    "prompt_version_id": "{{promptVersionId}}"
  }
}

docs {
  The shape an SDK tool loop sends: the caller rendered the prompt itself, so it
  passes its own `messages`, names the catalog tools by ref, and hands over the
  prompt version those messages came from.

  - `tool_refs[]` takes either `alias` (default `production`) or `version` to pin
    one exact build — both on one ref is a 400.
  - `prompt_version_id` stamps the request row and the `llm` span, so the trace
    links back to the prompt. It must be a prompt version in your own team;
    another team's id is a 400, not a silent drop.
  - Tool calls come back raw. Nothing is executed for you — that is what
    `run_prompt_with_tools()` in either SDK is for.
}
